From ef627e8e02ac49c79fd6c57dbad7b3cbd3c30557 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:52:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Web server: login lock per device, phone-app exemptions
 retired, the stock UI switch gone, 77 unused handlers removed

- Login lock (REAPER-LL-B1): the side backstop (20 failed logins on the LAN or WAN side within 300 s) is held in
  open code and asked by login_cgi only; while it holds, that side takes no new login for 300 s, but a signed-in
  admin keeps working and an address that logged in correctly before (and has not failed since) may still log in
  (16 per side, 7 days, memory only). A LAN IPv6 source is keyed by its whole address instead of its /64. The
  per-source lock (5 in 300 s) and the reply formats are unchanged.
- Login redirect: the typed address counts as the router's own name only while http_dut_redir is 1.
  (REAPER-DUT-REDIR-SELF)
- Requests that identify as the ASUS Router app no longer skip the cross-site refusal, the Referer rule or the page
  token, and apply.cgi refuses an apply by GET for every client. (REAPER-NOAPP-*)
- reaper_inject.c (native-UI cutover stage 5, REAPER-CUT8): the stock skin, the superseded-page bounce script and the
  reaper_inject kill switch are removed. A page httpd serves gets: a Reaper page the link floor and the shell bounce;
  the dashboard, shell, password page and first-boot Wi-Fi box the security banner; every other page the http_id
  token hook only; plus the colour-blind block when switched on. A missing .asp with a reaper_pagemap[] row (and,
  on a router that is not an AiMesh node, PrinterServer.asp / Advanced_TimeMachine.asp) is answered with a stub to
  the Reaper page; an AiMesh node gets no injection at all. New rows: index.asp, aimesh.asp, amesh.asp, clients.asp,
  gameboost.asp, gameprofile.asp, feedback_info.asp, sdn.asp. The index page is the dashboard.
- 77 handlers whose last caller was a removed stock page are gone (REAPER-UNUSED-CUT8): 48 page hooks, 22 file rows,
  4 pattern rows and 3 handlers with code, among them update.cgi (do_update_cgi ran any page hook named in ?output=
  with up to 16 arguments) and rog_first_qos.cgi; 38 functions, 4 helpers and their prototypes with them. Hooks that
  live only in closed objects lose their rows and extern lines. update.cgi and rog_first_qos.cgi join the
  removed-address log (one syslog line per name per boot). **.zip stays (a generic archive row add-ons can use).
- Earlier the same window: four hooks whose only callers were removed pages (ddns_info, dual_wanstate,
  get_tcfilter_array, wl_scan_5g_2) lost their rows. (REAPER-UNUSED-B6CD)
- defaults.c: reaper_cbmode (colour-blind mode, off). rmcpd / qos.c: the reaper_inject mentions removed.

